A||||7||Fformula88||Any Concrete experts here?||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||09-10-2001||04:50 PM||||Does anybody know anything about repairing concrete?  My garage floor has seen its better days.  The surface has all chipped off of it and has badly pitted the floor.  Is there any way to effectively and economically repair it so that it doesn't continue to deteriorate?<P>The constant cement dust is always covering everything... including (gasp) the Fiero if I leave it in there all day!  I gotta figure something out, but certainly cannot afford to have it taken out and re-poured!  (Its a 2 car garage)<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||09-10-2001||08:37 PM||||patch and paint but sounds like you got a bad batch and if it is to old [mix too long befor pored] or to dry a mix there is not a good way to fix and it will keep going bad.<BR>caps [lay overtop] need to be thick 2" or more or it will break up too.<BR>maybe a good rubber based paint will work for a time. swiming pool paint???<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-10-2001||10:17 PM||||Exoxy coating the floor ***may*** save you, if you use about twice the recomended thickness (get twice as much, and swather it on there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Costs about $400 for a normal size garrage, but it's SO GREAT!!!  I wouldn't even think about working on bare concreate ever again.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||09-10-2001||11:24 PM||||Im going to resurface my concrete in the garage.  Im waiting a month from now, when my crack repairs are cured, the crack repairs was a pain in the ass.<P>Quickrete sells a resurfacer for 20 bucks a bag.  You mix it up in a 5 gallon bucket and squeege it all over the concrete.<P>I will be doing this in beginning of oct.  You have to get a powerwasher and clean the cement and probably have to use muratic acid also.  After that i will use an epoxy from <A HREF="http://www.griotsgarage.com," TARGET=_blank>http://www.griotsgarage.com,</A>  that a fellow fiero owner recommended.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||10-18-2001||11:52 PM||||UPDATE:<P>I spent few days degreasing half of the garage floor.  I did it 3 times including an etcher/rust remover(1 time), which didn't seem to do anything.<P>I bought two bags of that quickrete resurfacer.  One bag did half of the garage, which i wanted. I spent about 3 hours laying it down.  I tried their floor squeegee idea, but didn't like it.  Im glad i bought that trowel to do the job.  <P>I used a 5 gallon bucket and mixed it with 3.3liters of water.  I couldn't afford to get a mixer, like they suggested(college student).  So i used a wooden rod from a broom.  To get some of the clumps, i stuck my hand in there, which isn't really suggested, and crushed the clumps.  The cement is like a milkshake, and feels like small BBs or fine grit, just an interesting sensation.<P>I poured half the bucket and squeeged.  I didn't really liked it and used the trowel.  When i did it, i thought, its going to turn out bad.  I smoothed 1/4 of the garage, and there were lines from the trowel.  I went back and smoothed it out.  I realized that i had to put pressure and remove the excess cement and the lines were disapearing.  I just kept on smoothing it out and it turned out like i wanted it too.<P>3 hours later and it looks sweet.  6 hours dry time to walk on, and 24 hours for vehicles.  Im going to put another coat on friday to make it really smooth and so all the pits will look invisible.<P>I cant wait till i paint it with griots epoxy paint.  Now i will be able to slide underneath my fiero.<P>Maybe xmas i can post pics, unless you guys want pics with a cheap dig camera, really low res.||||reg||1
Z||000005||gt boy||10-20-2001||12:36 AM||||artherd...what is this exoxy that you speak of??||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever3000||10-20-2001||12:40 AM||||I don't know about chips & pits, but don't the people who make Thompson's Water Seal for wood decks also make a garage floor surface treatment?  Thought I saw a commercial for it once.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierospeeder||10-20-2001||08:40 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.ucoatit.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ucoatit.com</A> <P>sells an epoxy paint that professionals use.  Its 250-300 dollars for a kit.<P>The people on Crank and chrome, the old cast from shadetree mechanic have it in their garage.  And a lot of companys use it also, there are some pics at that website.<P>The griots paint im going to use is a two part epoxy and its only 55 bucks.  If i had a brand new garage i would go with u coat it, but my garage is 25 years old and the concrete can crack again and i would be wasting a lot of money.||||reg||1
